  bootwright / controller uninstall
      Remove, on a host that holds no context and no installer media, the host packages
      controller install recorded as its own, through the host's own dnf, then Bootwright's
      state: /var/lib/bootwright and /var/lib/bootwright-staging. It never removes a package
      present before Bootwright, a package a controller stage installed, or this executable. It
      refuses before any effect while a context or an image remains, naming the commands that
      remove each, while another command holds the store, and, without --keep-packages, when
      the install record cannot say what install added or another installed package requires
      one of them. The plan shows dnf's own removal preview and what stays before confirmation.
      A host with nothing to remove prints Nothing to do. Review the plan before confirming;
      --yes skips ordinary confirmation.

  Usage
    bootwright controller uninstall [flags]

  Command flags
      --keep-packages  Leave every host package installed and remove only Bootwright's state
      --yes            Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  Examples
    bootwright controller uninstall
